# An allowlist: the build context holds only core/ and fetcher/, so nothing
# else in the checkout (a local .env, spike output, tests, .git) can reach an
# image layer. Both images share this context, and each Dockerfile copies only
# the paths it names (the fetcher image takes three files of core/).
*
!core
!fetcher
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
# Marks core/static/**/*.js as ES modules for `node --test` only. It is not in
# the static allowlist, so it is never served; leaving it out of the image
# keeps /app/core/static to the files the server actually loads.
core/static/package.json
